Installing imud
===============

Prerequisites (Raspberry Pi OS / Debian Bookworm or similar):

    sudo apt install build-essential libgpiod-dev

Build and install the core — the imud daemon plus imud-cal, imud-status,
imud-mon, the client libraries, the config, the systemd unit, and man pages:

    make
    sudo make install

Installs to /usr/local by default. Override the prefix, or stage into a
packaging root, with the standard variables:

    sudo make install PREFIX=/usr
    make install DESTDIR=/tmp/stage PREFIX=/usr        # staged, no root needed

Optional bridge daemons are built and installed separately — each is its own
package with its own dependencies, config, and docs:

    make bridges                                       # build all bridges
    sudo make install-signalk                          # Signal K bridge
    sudo make install-mqtt                             # MQTT bridge (needs libmosquitto-dev)
    sudo make install-influxdb                         # InfluxDB bridge
    sudo make install-mavlink                          # MAVLink bridge

Edit the configuration for your hardware, then enable the service:

    sudo nano /etc/imud/imud.conf
    sudo systemctl enable --now imud

Other targets:

    make test            # run the test suite (from the repo root)
    sudo make uninstall  # remove installed files (config in /etc/imud is kept)

The full installation, configuration, and calibration guide is docs/manual.md
(installed to /usr/share/doc/imud/manual.md).
